<title>FRANCE: ADP - Import traffic up 5.6pct in Feb 97.</title>
<headline>ADP - Import traffic up 5.6pct in Feb 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>February 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 43,068 tonnes, an increase of 5.6 percent on the same month the previous year, Aeroports de Paris,(ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Origin of global ADP imports in February 1997 with percentage change on February 1996, was as follows:  Domestic		  2,267   down  9.2pct</p>
<p> European Union	  5,268   up   23.6</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	   1,112   up   19.2</p>
<p> North Africa	    1,000   down 16.7</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    4,977   up    3.9</p>
<p> North America	  13,960   down  4.2</p>
<p> French territories    1,156   up   22.5</p>
<p> Latin America	   1,813   up   14.2</p>
<p> Middle East	     1,797   up    5.9</p>
<p> Far East		  9,718   up   17.2</p>
<p> Total		    43,068   up    5.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
